  "limits": [
    "One deterministic selection: official test indices0..2 warmup and3..10 timed for each dataset. Each timed sample runs once per model/mode; variation across samples is not repeated-run variability.",
    "GSM8K uses the original question. HumanEval uses a completion instruction plus the unchanged original prompt. Both use a shared chat wrapper and empty closed think prefix. Reference answers/solutions/tests are excluded from inputs.",
    "Output limit256 with normal EOS; actual lengths are preserved. Throughput is total generated tokens divided by total engine decode time, excluding loading, calibration and warmup.",
    "Three independent warmup samples precede every dataset/mode in a fresh model process. Initial targeted model-only fadvise is followed by loading and warmup; no all-model warming read or global cache drop.",
    "This is a warmed-workload comparison using the physical32GB card. Same target expert placement is fixed across modes for a model. It is not the earlier artificially small-cache or cold-cache sweep.",
    "The container cannot create a50GiB cgroup limit or disable swap.50GiB is a budget with a soft watchdog, not a kernel hard limit. Process RSS includes mapped pages and does not measure every unreferenced OS file-cache page.",
    "VRAM is full-device usage sampled every50ms, including driver and loading; short peaks may be missed. Native I/O counters have session-wide scopes including initialization and warmups; /proc request read_bytes is reported separately.",
    "Performance and same-model token parity were checked. No GSM8K accuracy score or HumanEval pass@1/code execution is claimed."
  ]
}
